---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, SITE_NAME, SITE_URL } from '../config/site.js';

const UPDATED = '10 June 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms and Conditions"
  description={`Terms of use for ${SITE_NAME}: acceptable use, accuracy disclaimer for the browser-based decibel meter, limitation of liability, and how to reach us.`}
>
  <section class="mx-auto w-full max-w-6xl px-4 sm:px-6 pt-10 sm:pt-14 pb-6">
    <p class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent-hover dark:text-accent-light">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink dark:text-dark-ink">
      Terms and Conditions
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-mute dark:text-dark-mute">Last updated {UPDATED}</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto w-full max-w-6xl px-4 sm:px-6 pb-16">
    <div class="prose-page">
      <p>
        These terms govern your use of {SITE_NAME} at {SITE_URL} (the
        “Service”). By using the Service you agree to them. If you do not
        agree, please do not use the Service.
      </p>

      <h2>1. The Service</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE_NAME} is a free, browser-based tool that estimates sound levels
        using your device’s microphone. It requires no account and no
        installation. We may modify, suspend, or discontinue any part of the
        Service at any time.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>You agree not to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>use the Service for any unlawful purpose or to harass others.</li>
        <li>
          attempt to disrupt, reverse-engineer for malicious purposes, or
          overload the Service.
        </li>
        <li>
          misrepresent readings produced by the Service as certified or
          legally admissible measurements.
        </li>
        <li>
          remove or obscure notices of ownership from the Service.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Accuracy disclaimer</h2>
      <p>
        Consumer microphones, device cases, and browser audio pipelines all
        affect readings. The Service provides an <strong>estimate</strong>
        intended for education, awareness, and relative comparison. It is
        <strong>not</strong> a certified sound level meter and must not be used
        for regulatory compliance, legal proceedings, occupational noise
        assessments, or any purpose requiring calibrated instrumentation.
        Results vary between devices even after calibration.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Health and safety</h2>
      <p>
        Readings shown by the Service are informational and do not constitute
        health or safety advice. You remain responsible for protecting your
        hearing and the hearing of others; when in doubt, reduce exposure to
        loud sound and consult official guidance.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        The Service, including its design, text, and code, is owned by us or
        our licensors and is protected by applicable copyright law. We grant
        you a limited, non-exclusive, revocable licence to use the Service for
        its intended purpose. You may not redistribute or resell the Service
        without written permission.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        The Service is provided “as is” and “as available”, without warranties
        of any kind, express or implied. To the maximum extent permitted by
        law, we exclude liability for indirect, incidental, or consequential
        damages arising from your use of the Service, including errors in
        readings, interruption of the Service, or loss of stored preferences.
        Our total liability shall not exceed the greater of the amount you
        paid us (nothing, in practice) in the twelve months before the claim.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Your use of the Service is also governed by our
        <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>, which explains how
        microphone audio and local preferences are handled.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms from time to time. Material changes will be
        reflected in the revision date above. Continued use of the Service
        after changes means you accept the updated terms.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of the jurisdiction in which the
        operating entity is established, without regard to conflict-of-law
        rules.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms? Email
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
